% The \textwidth command in twocolumn mode gives the full width of the text along the wholse page.
% If one wants to have the `actual' text width, then it'll have to be reduced.
% I don't know wether if there is already an apporpriate command. 
% I don't even know how much exactly I have to reduce it. 
% But it poses problem and this is the way I found to fix it.
\newlength{\actualtextwidth}
\if@twocolumn
      \setlength{\actualtextwidth}{0.5\textwidth - \columnsep - 0.5\columnseprule}
\else
      \setlength{\actualtextwidth}{\textwidth}
\fi
